# Everything the image builds for itself, plus everything it must never carry.
#
# .env is the important line. The build context is this repo; a stray .env
# copied into a layer would put our production secrets on a client's box, where
# their ops team has root — and layers survive a later `rm`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
Cashfree_*.csv
.places-key.tmp

node_modules
.next
.git
.github
.claude

# Built on the VM, not shipped.
vaani-src.tar.gz
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Sales collateral, lead lists and call recordings: not runtime, and the leads
# are personal data that has no business in a client's image.
sales
design
voice-test
tests
docs
*.md
!README.md
